	(text "HOW IT CONNECTS (rev B, simple)\nJ1 (1x2) and J2 (1x1) are standard 2.54 mm straight male headers, hand-soldered by the builder (3 joints).\nPins are numbered by the J6 pin they mate: 5 = LED_SW (anode bus), 6 = W- (warm return), 11 = C- (cool return).\nEvery other J6 position (incl. J6-12 P+_FUSE and J6-4 GND) has NO pin and no hole on this board.\nHeader: body 2.5 / post 6.0 / tail 3.0; post tips at Y 108.10 -> J6 engagement 4.72..5.05 mm.\n\nEACH STRING: LED_SW -> 5 LEDs -> Rs 200 R (CRCW0805200RFKEAHP) -> W-/C-. No series diode (rev B):\nthe housing keys the plug; with 200 R the main board is safe in every misinsertion (research/electrical-j6.md sec 5).\nDriver: constant current 13.3 mA (14.0 max), one string at a time; OVP 24.25 V min; design ceiling 22.0 V.\nString at 13.3 mA: 5 x Vf 13.0..15.8 V + Rs 2.66 V = LED_SW 16.0..19.4 V (typ 17.3 V, incl. sense + FET) < 22.0 V.\nHot-plug peak through Rs 200 R: TPS923610 47..53 mA, TPS923611 71..77 mA < IFP 80 mA.\n\nLEDs: HONGLITRONIC HL-A-3014H421W-S1-08HL-HR3; the MPN does not encode CCT: warm D1-D5 = LCSC C210340 (3000 K),\ncool D6-D10 = LCSC C210343 (6000 K). Pad 1 (large) = cathode. Do not plug the bare board into J6 (no housing = no key)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 116.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c8629b3f-70eb-5057-a36c-9d0388a66670"))
